# GUI features must localize (hard rule)

Operator directive (Phil, 2026-08-22), verbatim intent:

> **When implementing new features for the GUI, always build it with
> localization of all strings. Build US English and German support in
> localization, and provide a plan for missing translations.**

## The rule

> **New GUI features ship every operator-visible string through locale
> catalogs — never hardcoded English-only TSX. US English (`en`) and
> German (`de`) land in the same change set. Missing translations are
> a recorded plan (localization-work queue), not a later surprise.
> Agent draft catalogs do not close the item.**

## Same change set

| Required | Forbidden |
| --- | --- |
| New chrome keys in `en` **and** `de` | English-only new buttons, hints, dialogs, empty states |
| Queue row in `core-assets/content/localization-work/` | “We’ll translate later” with no queue item |
| Status **open** until required tags are reviewed | Closing on agent DE drafts |

## Plan for missing translations

Record `required_tags` for remaining Tier 1 (`en-GB`, `zh-Hans`, `zh-TW`)
and any other shipped tags. Notes state: data add later, not a code
rewrite. Do **not** close the item when only draft `de` exists.

